.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-ACCEPT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-accept - Accept an invitation bound to this account


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team accept <invitation> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Accept an invitation bound to this account

.PP
Accept an invitation explicitly addressed to this account. The resulting membership does not automatically grant access to every resource owned or shared by the team.

.PP
Teams use explicit membership and resource grants. Membership alone does not grant machine use, ENV values, previews, or tunnels. Mutations use the current team generation to reject stale edits; read pb team get before retrying a conflicting change.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for accept

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team(1)\fP
